    "This is a Portuguese man o' war! It looks like a jellyfish, but it's not! It's a team of tiny animals stuck together, and each one has its own job. A team of tiny animals living together is called a colony. Its long tentacles sting, so look, but don't touch!": "a99d7b897872.mp3",
    "This is a blue whale! The blue whale is the biggest animal that has ever lived, even bigger than the dinosaurs! The biggest animal in the world eats some of the tiniest! Blue whales gulp up tiny krill.": "d0d8c676bb8e.mp3",
    "This is a clownfish! Clownfish are orange with white stripes. Clownfish eat plankton and leftovers from their anemone home.": "b37a094f6d34.mp3",
    "This is a crab! Crabs walk sideways! Crabs eat almost anything, even leftovers.": "26eb6dfb222e.mp3",
    "This is a dolphin! A dolphin is not a fish. It breathes air through a blowhole on top of its head. Dolphins eat fish and squid. They swim up to the top to breathe air!": "2678a0fb5dfd.mp3",
    "This is a flying fish! When a hungry fish chases it, a flying fish zooms out of the water and glides through the air on its big, wing-like fins! Flying fish don't flap like birds. They glide, like a paper airplane, to get away from fish that want to eat them!": "0ddb39e11028.mp3",
    "This is a great white shark! Great white sharks are the biggest hunting fish in the sea. Great whites eat big fish, like tuna, and seals. Only orcas hunt great white sharks.": "e6892f57a855.mp3",
    "This is a hammerhead shark! A hammerhead's head is wide and flat, like a hammer, with an eye at each end. It can see above and below at the same time! Hammerheads love to eat stingrays. They find them hiding under the sand by feeling their electricity!": "1a4ab2115cb0.mp3",
    "This is a horseshoe crab! A horseshoe crab isn't really a crab! It's more like a cousin of spiders and scorpions. Horseshoe crabs have blue blood! Doctors use it to check that medicines are safe.": "8c31ff172152.mp3",
    "This is a jellyfish! A jellyfish is not a fish! It has no brain, no heart and no bones. Jellyfish catch tiny plankton with their stinging tentacles. Sea turtles love to eat jellyfish!": "c4aae7b26286.mp3",
    "This is a lobster! A lobster has a hard shell and ten legs. The front two are big claws. Lobsters walk along the sea floor and eat crabs, clams and sea urchins.": "25c31e2d69fd.mp3",
    "This is a mackerel! Mackerel are fast fish with wavy stripes on their backs. Mackerel eat plankton and little fish, like sardines. Squid, tuna and sharks eat mackerel.": "6cf3070676c9.mp3",
    "This is a manta ray! Manta rays flap their wide fins like wings. They look like they're flying underwater! Manta rays swim with their mouths wide open to scoop up tiny plankton.": "335f843935fd.mp3",
    "This is a mantis shrimp! A mantis shrimp punches faster than you can blink! Its punch can crack a crab's shell. Mantis shrimp have one of the fastest punches of any animal. Smash! They crack open crabs and snails to eat what's inside.": "5d1dca876097.mp3",
    "This is a moray eel! A moray eel looks like a snake, but it's a fish! It hides in holes in the reef. Moray eels open and close their mouths all the time. They aren't being grumpy. They're breathing!": "94875ec73b3a.mp3",
    "This is a narwhal! Some people call it the unicorn of the sea. A narwhal is a small whale that lives in the icy Arctic Ocean, near the North Pole. A narwhal's tusk is a tooth that can grow longer than a grown-up is tall! Narwhals breathe air, so they come up through cracks in the ice.": "2435eb9d5eab.mp3",
    "This is a parrotfish! Parrotfish have teeth shaped like a parrot's beak. Parrotfish eat algae that grows on coral. Lots of white beach sand is parrotfish poop!": "1e380561cbdc.mp3",
    "This is a penguin! A penguin is a bird, but it can't fly in the air. It flies underwater instead, flapping its wings like flippers! Penguins dive down to catch fish, krill and squid. They're birds, so they pop back up to breathe air!": "6a6fb8903238.mp3",
    "This is a pufferfish! When a pufferfish is scared, it gulps water and puffs up into a big spiky ball! Pufferfish crunch crabs and clams with their strong teeth. Look, but don't touch!": "ce058c5de5bd.mp3",
    "This is a sardine! Sardines are small, shiny, silver fish. Sardines eat tiny plankton. Mackerel, squid, tuna and sharks eat sardines.": "0be08b72e1ec.mp3",
    "This is a sea cucumber! A sea cucumber is an animal, not a vegetable! It's a cousin of sea stars and sea urchins. When some sea cucumbers get scared, they squirt their insides out to scare the hungry animal away. Then they grow new ones!": "1561f8126ecf.mp3",
    "This is a sea otter! Sea otters have the thickest fur of any animal. It keeps them warm in cold water. Sea otters eat lots of sea urchins, and sea urchins eat kelp. So sea otters help kelp forests grow!": "73975ed96db9.mp3",
    "This is a sea star! Some people call it a starfish. A sea star is not a fish. Most sea stars have five arms. Sea stars eat clams. They push their tummy out of their mouth to eat!": "75fe78418ab2.mp3",
    "This is a sea turtle! Sea turtles have a hard shell and flippers for swimming. Some sea turtles eat sea grass. Some eat jellyfish!": "09e1656a09db.mp3",
    "This is a sea urchin! A sea urchin is a spiky ball. Its spikes keep it safe. Sea urchins munch on seaweed. Sea otters, lobsters and pufferfish eat sea urchins.": "c78254942cbf.mp3",
    "This is a seahorse! A seahorse is a fish with a head shaped like a horse. It holds on to seaweed with its curly tail. Seahorses slurp up tiny shrimp with their long snouts.": "fe12beaa0b5d.mp3",
    "This is a squid! A squid is not a fish! It has a soft body and ten arms. Squid grab little fish, like sardines and mackerel, with their arms. Tuna and sharks eat squid.": "7efd0114d96f.mp3",
    "This is a tuna! Tuna are big fish and super-fast swimmers. Tuna eat fish, like mackerel, and squid. Big sharks and orcas eat tuna.": "0613c34aed48.mp3",
    "This is a whale shark! A whale shark is not a whale. It's a shark, and the biggest fish in the whole ocean! Whale sharks are gentle giants. They swim with their huge mouths open and sieve tiny plankton out of the water. Animals that eat like that are called filter feeders.": "b818ed578c65.mp3",
    "This is an anglerfish! An anglerfish has a fishing rod growing on its head, with a wiggly lure on the end to trick little fish. When a little fish swims up to the lure, gulp! Deep-sea anglerfish have lures that glow in the dark. Light made by living things is called bioluminescence.": "1341d4db2da5.mp3",
    "This is an octopus! An octopus has eight arms covered in suckers. Octopuses love to eat crabs.": "f5983ad2f954.mp3",
    "This is an orca! Some people call it a killer whale. Orcas are black and white. They are the biggest dolphins in the world! Orcas eat fish, seals, and even great white sharks. Nothing hunts orcas!": "02a0e7e5b587.mp3",
    "This is plankton! Plankton are tiny living things that drift in the sea. Most are too small to see! Plant plankton make their food from sunlight, like trees. Lots of animals eat plankton, even giant whales!": "398ef8218573.mp3",
